<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Mr. Dostoevsky returns three weeks after coming home from two months abroad. About four weeks ago, in a spa town he had not planned to visit, he went into a casino and played roulette on four evenings over one week, losing about two months of his income; he borrowed money to come home. On the second of those nights he stayed at the tables until morning and missed his evening lamotrigine dose, then missed it again the next evening. The following morning he had a generalized tonic-clonic seizure in his hotel room, witnessed by a member of staff, lasting about two minutes; he bit his tongue and was confused for some hours. He was checked in a local emergency department and released the same day; he brought the discharge letter, which records a normal examination and no injury. He has taken every dose since and has had no further seizure. He did not tell the clinic until today, because he felt ashamed. He had arranged no telehealth therapy sessions before leaving and had none while away. He has not gambled since he came home three weeks ago. He feels ashamed and worried about the new debt but says he has no thoughts of suicide and wants to get back on track. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Seizure</td><td>One generalized seizure about four weeks ago, after a night awake at the tables and two missed doses</td></tr><tr><td>Gambling</td><td>Roulette on four evenings abroad; large loss; none for three weeks</td></tr><tr><td>Therapy</td><td>No sessions during the two months away</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>PHQ-9 9, GAD-7 8; no thoughts of suicide</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

